 "voice": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "t": 0.1,
   "dur": 4.061,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "What's this cell carrying? Room for about a billion passengers."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 5.1,
   "dur": 9.107,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "It's packed with one protein, hemoglobin: about two hundred and seventy million copies. Each one has four iron atoms, and each can hold an oxygen."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 15.1,
   "dur": 8.919,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "Watch one fill. The first oxygen struggles to board, but each one makes the next one easier. Dark red at the start; full, it's bright red."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 25.1,
   "dur": 12.309,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "Veins often look blue, so it's easy to guess the blood inside them is. It never is. Returning blood is darker red. Red light sinks in, and the vein swallows it, so less red comes back."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 40.3,
   "dur": 9.731,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "Your heart sends your blood back through your lungs about once a minute. There, the empty seats fill. In about a quarter of a second."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "t": 53.9,
   "dur": 5.489,
   "file": "vo/06.wav",
   "text": "The blue is your skin's trick. The red is a passenger count: brighter means fuller seats."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "t": 60.3,
   "dur": 4.684,
   "file": "vo/07.wav",
   "text": "Meanwhile, as you watched, your blood handed your body about a cup of oxygen."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo08",
   "t": 65.9,
   "dur": 4.733,
   "file": "vo/08.wav",
   "text": "Next: the signal in your nerves. In the fastest, it doesn't crawl; it jumps."
  }
 ]
}